WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.228
- I am pretty excited that
we get to have some wine.

00:00:02.228 --> 00:00:04.228
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.228 --> 00:00:06.180
Mmm, that is excellent.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.270
Hey guys, it's Katie

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:08.790
and for the next 14 days,

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.680
I'm gonna be trying out
the Mediterranean Diet.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.280
I've actually been wanting to
do this for a very long time

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.960
because it actually seems
more like a lifestyle change

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.140
than a super restrictive way of eating.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.810
And it apparently has many health benefits

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.040
such as increasing life expectancy,

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.850
reducing major chronic diseases

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.260
and improving your quality
of life and well-being.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:29.599
There's been celebrities
that have also attested

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:32.050
to its health benefits like Selena Gomez,

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.220
Penelope Cruz and John Goodman.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.250
I kinda wanna undo some bad habits

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.496
that I've created over the last two years

00:00:37.496 --> 00:00:39.910
in quarantine, out of quarantine

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.980
and just commit to my
health and happiness.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.541
So to get started, I
spoke with a dietician.

00:00:43.541 --> 00:00:45.771
And basically the Mediterranean Diet

00:00:45.771 --> 00:00:48.540
is an eating plan based on
the traditional cuisines

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.110
of Greece, Italy and other countries

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.780
surrounding the Mediterranean sea.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.930
It's mainly plant-based

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:56.150
and emphasizes the intake of whole grains,

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:57.310
fruits and vegetables,

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:58.920
healthy fats, such as olive oil,

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.340
as well as nuts and legumes,

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.520
over the intake of animal protein,

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.770
which is usually served
in smaller portions.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.250
Typically fish or seafood
is the preferred meat.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.210
And it's also about your lifestyle.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:12.140
So sharing meals with
others, not watching the TV

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.170
or being on the computer
when you're eating,

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:15.690
being present and connected

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:18.300
and also partaking in daily
activities that you like.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.900
Like walking your dog or riding a bicycle.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.900
The things to avoid on this
diet are processed foods,

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.090
refined grains and
foods with added sugars,

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.520
which is gonna be hard for me.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.410
While alcohol is usually
for just special occasions,

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:34.720
you can have a glass of red
wine a night if you like.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.690
Which I would like.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:36.960
I think this is doable.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.280
I'm gonna try my best, so lets try it.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.050
So day one of this diet
started a little bit rough.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.510
Okay, so I was supposed to go shopping

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:44.810
and meal prep last night,

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.500
but I ended up sitting in
about 10 hours of traffic.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.670
So I just really didn't
feel like doing it.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.960
So today I'm gonna see
what I have in my pantry

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.060
and then go to the store, do shopping

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.930
and get myself set up
for the rest of the week.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.030
So that morning for breakfast,

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:58.980
I basically had to just
look around my kitchen,

00:01:58.980 --> 00:01:59.813
see what I had

00:01:59.813 --> 00:02:03.540
